{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00410",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 0.8,
      "end_seconds": 6.17,
      "duration_seconds": 5.37,
      "text": "All set here, doctor. Chart's updated, and I'll read the readings out when you're ready."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 10.12,
      "end_seconds": 14.24,
      "duration_seconds": 4.12,
      "text": "Right, thank you. Good morning, tell me what's been going on."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 15.49,
      "end_seconds": 19.64,
      "duration_seconds": 4.15,
      "text": "Hello, doctor, I came in with them, if that's okay."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 20.93,
      "end_seconds": 24.24,
      "duration_seconds": 3.31,
      "text": "Alright, yes, that's no problem at all. Please sit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 24.76,
      "end_seconds": 29.2,
      "duration_seconds": 4.44,
      "text": "Yeah, it's yellow eyes. I don't know what's causing it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 30.16,
      "end_seconds": 32.28,
      "duration_seconds": 2.12,
      "text": "When did you first notice it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 33.2,
      "end_seconds": 35.26,
      "duration_seconds": 2.06,
      "text": "For three days, I'd say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 35.96,
      "end_seconds": 42.04,
      "duration_seconds": 6.08,
      "text": "And the other thing I wanted to mention is that I can't really—"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 42.14,
      "end_seconds": 46.23,
      "duration_seconds": 4.09,
      "text": "Tell the doctor about the other thing, that's what worries me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 46.87,
      "end_seconds": 48.73,
      "duration_seconds": 1.86,
      "text": "I was getting to that!"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 49.26,
      "end_seconds": 53.02,
      "duration_seconds": 3.76,
      "text": "That's fine, one at a time. I'll ask about everything."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 53.8,
      "end_seconds": 55.9,
      "duration_seconds": 2.1,
      "text": "And itching all over, too."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 56.58,
      "end_seconds": 59.48,
      "duration_seconds": 2.9,
      "text": "Is it constant, or does it come and go?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 59.99,
      "end_seconds": 61.54,
      "duration_seconds": 1.55,
      "text": "It's all the time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 62.01,
      "end_seconds": 66.68,
      "duration_seconds": 4.67,
      "text": "Have you had yellow eyes before, or is this the first time?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 68.05,
      "end_seconds": 73.17,
      "duration_seconds": 5.12,
      "text": "I had a similar thing a couple of years ago. It went away."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 73.54,
      "end_seconds": 75.31,
      "duration_seconds": 1.77,
      "text": "Have you had any confusion?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 76.11,
      "end_seconds": 77.51,
      "duration_seconds": 1.4,
      "text": "No, no confusion."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 78.56,
      "end_seconds": 80.25,
      "duration_seconds": 1.69,
      "text": "And fever, any of that?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 81.16,
      "end_seconds": 82.61,
      "duration_seconds": 1.45,
      "text": "No, no fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 83.93,
      "end_seconds": 88.29,
      "duration_seconds": 4.36,
      "text": "Actually, doctor, I did notice fever. She doesn't always say."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 88.77,
      "end_seconds": 93.85,
      "duration_seconds": 5.08,
      "text": "No, I don't think I did. Maybe a little, I'm not sure."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 94.49,
      "end_seconds": 102.87,
      "duration_seconds": 8.38,
      "text": "Alright, I'll note both what you've said and what you've noticed. Okay, have you had any weight loss, black stools or swelling of the tummy?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 107.0,
      "end_seconds": 118.17,
      "duration_seconds": 11.17,
      "text": "No, no weight loss, no black stools, no swelling of the tummy. I did have dark urine at one point, but that went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 119.17,
      "end_seconds": 121.41,
      "duration_seconds": 2.24,
      "text": "Any problems with your joints or muscles?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 122.37,
      "end_seconds": 124.25,
      "duration_seconds": 1.88,
      "text": "No, joints are fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 124.71,
      "end_seconds": 136.18,
      "duration_seconds": 11.47,
      "text": "Doctor, I've got the readings for you. SpO2 99 percent on room air, weight 60 kilos, pulse is 85 beats a minute, blood pressure 114 over 77, height 166 centimetres."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 139.36,
      "end_seconds": 143.7,
      "duration_seconds": 4.34,
      "text": "Thanks. Do you have any allergies to medicines, food, anything at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 144.98,
      "end_seconds": 149.4,
      "duration_seconds": 4.42,
      "text": "I'm allergic to penicillin, I get swelling of my face."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 150.57,
      "end_seconds": 152.59,
      "duration_seconds": 2.02,
      "text": "Does anything run in the family?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 153.91,
      "end_seconds": 157.5,
      "duration_seconds": 3.59,
      "text": "My grandmother had breast cancer. My father was diabetic."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 158.68,
      "end_seconds": 161.46,
      "duration_seconds": 2.78,
      "text": "Has anything about your daily routine changed lately?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 162.77,
      "end_seconds": 177.57,
      "duration_seconds": 14.8,
      "text": "Not really, the days are pretty much the same, work and home, and I've been trying to fit appointments in around my schedule, which isn't always easy, so I'm glad we could find a time today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 178.44,
      "end_seconds": 183.6,
      "duration_seconds": 5.16,
      "text": "Any long-term health problems I should know about? Take your time, there's no rush."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 184.81,
      "end_seconds": 196.48,
      "duration_seconds": 11.67,
      "text": "Uh, I have diabetes. I'd rather not end up on lots of tablets if I can avoid it. High cholesterol, for about ten years. Heart disease, for five years."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 197.79,
      "end_seconds": 206.59,
      "duration_seconds": 8.8,
      "text": "Okay, high cholesterol, that's already on your record. Good to know. Yes, I can see the heart disease in your file as well. Any previous surgeries?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 207.51,
      "end_seconds": 211.24,
      "duration_seconds": 3.73,
      "text": "Yes, I had a bypass operation, six years ago."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 211.72,
      "end_seconds": 213.25,
      "duration_seconds": 1.53,
      "text": "And alcohol, how much?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 213.82,
      "end_seconds": 217.95,
      "duration_seconds": 4.13,
      "text": "A beer or two most evenings, to be honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0040",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 218.68,
      "end_seconds": 222.32,
      "duration_seconds": 3.64,
      "text": "Any medication at the moment, including things from the pharmacy?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0041",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 222.81,
      "end_seconds": 226.51,
      "duration_seconds": 3.7,
      "text": "I'm on Glycomet, 500 milligrams, twice a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0042",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "FAMILY_MEMBER",
      "start_seconds": 228.0,
      "end_seconds": 235.83,
      "duration_seconds": 7.83,
      "text": "Doctor, I think the last prescription for the Glycomet was 250 milligrams. We changed it at the last visit."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0043",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 236.32,
      "end_seconds": 240.08,
      "duration_seconds": 3.76,
      "text": "Okay. Have you got the newest prescription or the box with you?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0044",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 240.95,
      "end_seconds": 251.6,
      "duration_seconds": 10.65,
      "text": "Not with me. I'll bring it next time. Rosuvastatin, 10 milligrams, at night. I've never really been one for hospitals. I did try to ignore it for a while."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0045",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 252.01,
      "end_seconds": 254.57,
      "duration_seconds": 2.56,
      "text": "How long have you been on it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0046",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 255.72,
      "end_seconds": 257.25,
      "duration_seconds": 1.53,
      "text": "About a month now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0047",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 257.49,
      "end_seconds": 258.19,
      "duration_seconds": 0.7,
      "text": "Mm-hm."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0048",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 259.0,
      "end_seconds": 277.07,
      "duration_seconds": 18.07,
      "text": "I take aspirin, 75 milligrams, once a day. I'm hoping you can tell me something definite. I wasn't sure whether to come in at all, to be honest. Yeah, I'd been on atorvastatin, not any more though, I stopped."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0049",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 278.13,
      "end_seconds": 281.86,
      "duration_seconds": 3.73,
      "text": "I'll try to keep this as efficient as I can."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0050",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 283.27,
      "end_seconds": 285.54,
      "duration_seconds": 2.27,
      "text": "Thank you, I appreciate it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0051",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 287.09,
      "end_seconds": 289.99,
      "duration_seconds": 2.9,
      "text": "I'll examine you now, so please bear with me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0052",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 291.81,
      "end_seconds": 293.86,
      "duration_seconds": 2.05,
      "text": "Can you lie back for me?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0053",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 301.37,
      "end_seconds": 303.53,
      "duration_seconds": 2.16,
      "text": "The whites of your eyes are yellow."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0054",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 304.05,
      "end_seconds": 304.92,
      "duration_seconds": 0.87,
      "text": "Yes, doctor."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0055",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 306.78,
      "end_seconds": 309.75,
      "duration_seconds": 2.97,
      "text": "A little pressure here, tell me if it's tender."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0056",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 321.42,
      "end_seconds": 323.9,
      "duration_seconds": 2.48,
      "text": "Liver edge is just palpable and mildly tender."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0057",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 327.75,
      "end_seconds": 346.71,
      "duration_seconds": 18.96,
      "text": "Okay, you can sit back up. So, based on the history and the examination, it fits best with jaundice with a cause we still need to find. The reason I say that is that your story and my examination fit together. I can't rule out a gallstone blocking the bile duct yet."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0058",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 347.17,
      "end_seconds": 349.28,
      "duration_seconds": 2.11,
      "text": "Is it something serious, doctor?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0059",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 350.02,
      "end_seconds": 367.13,
      "duration_seconds": 17.11,
      "text": "It's reasonable to be concerned, but right now jaundice with a cause we still need to find is my leading thought, not anything worse. Let me just recap so I've got it right. You've had yellow eyes for three days, and no swelling of the tummy."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0060",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 368.28,
      "end_seconds": 371.03,
      "duration_seconds": 2.75,
      "text": "Exactly, uh, that's what's been happening."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0061",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 371.44,
      "end_seconds": 398.73,
      "duration_seconds": 27.29,
      "text": "Let's get an ultrasound of the abdomen, for jaundice. I'm going to order a hepatitis screen, for jaundice. That will help us see what's going on underneath and decide the next step. Please avoid alcohol completely and don't take any painkillers except paracetamol, and not much of that. Cut back on tea, coffee and fizzy drinks for a couple of weeks and see how things settle. I'll also refer you to a liver specialist."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0062",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 400.06,
      "end_seconds": 407.36,
      "duration_seconds": 7.3,
      "text": "And please bring the latest prescription or the medicine boxes to the next visit, so we can settle the dose."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0063",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 408.65,
      "end_seconds": 411.04,
      "duration_seconds": 2.39,
      "text": "Okay, um, I will."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0064",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 411.81,
      "end_seconds": 418.55,
      "duration_seconds": 6.74,
      "text": "I want you to come back or go to emergency straight away if you vomit blood or become drowsy or confused."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0065",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 419.32,
      "end_seconds": 421.14,
      "duration_seconds": 1.82,
      "text": "Yes, I'll do that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0066",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 421.89,
      "end_seconds": 427.19,
      "duration_seconds": 5.3,
      "text": "Let's review you in three days. That's everything on my side. Anything you're unsure about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0067",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 428.02,
      "end_seconds": 430.44,
      "duration_seconds": 2.42,
      "text": "Thank you. I'll see you then."
    }
  ]
}